<title>UK: Key economic forecasts from British budget.</title>
<headline>Key economic forecasts from British budget.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following are key  economic forecasts from the 1997/98 budget presented by Chancellor of the Exchequer Gordon Brown on Wednesday.</p>
<p>								 FORECAST</p>
<p>1996 1997 1998</p>
<p>OUTPUT AT CONSTANT PRICES</p>
<p>Gross domestic product(GDP)     2.5    3.25    2.5</p>
<p>Non-North Sea GDP		   2.5    3.25    2.5</p>
<p>Manufacturing output		0.25   1.5     0.75</p>
<p>EXPENDITURE COMPONENTS OF GDP AT CONSTANT PRICES</p>
<p>Domestic demand		     2.75   3.75    3.25</p>
<p>    Consumers' expenditure	3.5    4.5     4.0</p>
<p>    General govt. consumption   2.5   -0.25   -1.0</p>
<p>    Fixed investment		1.75   5.0     6.0</p>
<p>    Change in stockbuilding    -0.25   0.0     0.0</p>
<p>Exports of goods and services   7.0    6.25    5.0</p>
<p>Imports of goods and services   8.5    7.25    7.75</p>
<p>BALANCE OF PAYMENTS C/A</p>
<p> billion			    -0.5   -6.0    -9.0</p>
<p>percent of GDP			0.0   -0.75   -1.0</p>
<p>INFLATION</p>
<p>RPI ex-mortgage interest payments</p>
<p>(fourth quarter)		   3.25   2.5    2.75</p>
<p>Producer output prices</p>
<p>(Q4 ex food/bev/tob/petrol)    0.75   0.0    2.5</p>
<p>GDP deflator at market prices</p>
<p>(financial year)		   2.75   2.75   2.75</p>
<p>MONEY GDP AT MARKET PRICES</p>
<p>(FINANCIAL YEAR) billion	752    798    838</p>
<p>percentage change		  5.5    6.0    5.0</p>
<p>PSBR (FINANCIAL YEAR)</p>
<p> billion			    22.7   10.9    4.0</p>
<p>PSBR excluding windfall tax    22.7   13.3    5.4</p>
<p>PSBR ex windfall as pct/GDP    3.0    1.75   0.75</p>
<p>-- London newsroom 44 171 542 2774</p>
</text>
